<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Baqa Khalid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1311</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Baqa Khalid was a Hafsid prince who ruled the Hafsid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> from 1301, succeeding his father Abu Zakariya. In 1309 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> and reunited the two Hafsid realms as sultan, but his rule there was brief: he was overthrown and killed in 1311. Bejaia and Constantine later broke away again under other princes of the dynasty.</p></div>
